A||||22||8Ball||Coolant Leak please help!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||8Ball||08-29-2001||03:26 PM||||Ok I have been desperatly trying to get my Fiero on the road but have noticed a MAJOR coolant leak. I pour it in and it comes back out almost as quick as I can add it.<P>The best I can tell it LOOKS like it is coming from the water pump. But due to the way it is spilling and the speed I can't tell if it is comeing from the pully shaft on the water pump or if it is mearly running there from somewhere else. Does it sound right that the pump would leak at the shaft?<BR>Also is there anything I should check befor I go ripping this thing off?<P>Please help me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I wanna make the run for the hills in a month. That and I need this car driving.<P>Thanks, <BR>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||03:34 PM||||Ahh yea it could be leaking from the pump shaft  thats usually where they will leak from when they go bad at the seal and theres what they call a weep hole where it is actually leaking from on the bottom of the shaft housing ||||reg||1
Z||000002||8Ball||08-29-2001||03:40 PM||||Ok thanks,<BR>So now I guess I need to buy a water pump, find some good instructions on easily changeing it and get to work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Thanks,<BR>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000003||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||03:46 PM||||Randy what car year motor type etc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||8Ball||08-29-2001||03:46 PM||||86 se 2m6 2.8l v6||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||08-29-2001||03:47 PM||||If its a duke motor chances are it's the heater hose leaking at the nipple. The previous owners of my car had this happen and sold me the car because of it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000006||Formula88||08-29-2001||03:53 PM||||Make sure to get a new water pump with a metal impeller, and not a remanufactured one with a plastic impeller.  I've heard on here that the plastic impellers can't hold up to the pressure of pushing the coolent back and forth from the front mounted radiator.  In a FWD car, the coolent path is much shorter, so it's not as much of a strain on the pump.||||reg||1
Z||000007||8Ball||08-29-2001||03:56 PM||||I called one of the autozones in town, and they have a remanuf with 1 yr warrenty and metal impellor for 13.95. So I will prolly do that as I am job hunting AGAIN and on a very tight budget.<BR>Plus one way or the other I have to get the car fixed cause if I amnot makeing some finacial headway by the end of sept. I am selling the car and moveing back to canada<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||04:00 PM||||ok if you are gonna do the water pump .Iv e never had the pleasure of doing one . but none the less I ve prepared my self for that joyus occassion.The way I see it on the v-6 you have to remove the right wheel And the rubber skirt inside the wheel well to get access to some of the bolts And  you may have to remove battery tray too. it looks to me that is about 3 maybe 4 hour job hope fully some one else will jump in here to let us know of any surprises that are not explained by my brief explanation||||reg||1
Z||000009||TONY_C||08-29-2001||04:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 8Ball:<BR><B>Ok I have been desperatly trying to get my Fiero on the road but have noticed a MAJOR coolant leak. I pour it in and it comes back out almost as quick as I can add it.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know all is possible with our beloved two-seater but i can't imagine water pouring out as fast as that from the weep hole on the water pump.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Wolfhound||08-29-2001||06:35 PM||||Try using a mirror and flashlight to see that the water is coming from the weep hole. <P>One of the mirror on a stick things should come as standard equipment with every Fiero. ||||reg||1
